MID_EV12_027_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_027_m01_001: Excuse me. I would speak to you about your sword...\nIt is familiar to me.
MID_EV12_027_m01_002: <NCA>Let him see it.
MID_EV12_027_m01_003: Are you of Fódlan?
MID_EV12_027_m01_004: Indeed I am. Ah, so it is Answerer. You are of House\nLamine, I see.
MID_EV12_027_m01_005: Dietrich Gregor Lamine. I was in a shipwreck and\narrived here by chance alone.
MID_EV12_027_m01_006: You're...notorious. The Lailon Valley Massacre. I've\nheard of that, and that is scarcely all I have heard.
MID_EV12_027_m01_007: I'd hazard a guess you're to blame for the little scuffle\nthat earned Marquis Ribas's wrath.
MID_EV12_027_m01_008: As I watched your match, I couldn't help but notice\nthat a Hero's Relic had made its way to Dagda.
MID_EV12_027_m01_009: I see that you have a vicious look about you. The\nair of a blood-starved beast, in fact.
MID_EV12_027_m01_010: So you tracked and hunted me. Well done.
MID_EV12_027_m01_011: And now that I have cornered you, perhaps I can\nmake you listen.
MID_EV12_027_m01_012: Your technique is severe. You aim only to destroy\nyour opponents.
MID_EV12_027_m01_013: You wield the sword for your own pleasure, and you\ntake genuine delight in killing people.
MID_EV12_027_m01_014: You're no different than the 10 Elites of Fódlan, who\nplaced value only in the superiority of their strength.
MID_EV12_027_m01_015: <NCA>Allow for the possibility.
MID_EV12_027_m01_016: <NCB>Deny it.
MID_EV12_027_m01_017: <ACA>Perhaps so.
MID_EV12_027_m01_018: <ACA>If you continue on this road, you will put not just\nyourself, but those around you, in danger.
MID_EV12_027_m01_019: <ACA>I advise you to consider taking a different path. This\none leads only to ruin.
MID_EV12_027_m01_020: <ACB>So you say. Yet I doubt your words.
MID_EV12_027_m01_021: <ACB>I have difficulty with people like you. Waging\nneedless battles, stealing lives.
MID_EV12_027_m01_022: <ACB>No matter the era, the powerless get swept up in\nthis pointless bloodshed.
MID_EV12_027_m01_023: When you speak of the Elites, you sound as though\nyou know them very well.
MID_EV12_027_m01_024: Well, I have confidence in my judgment...and\nlet there be no mistake. You are a true killer.
MID_EV12_027_m01_025: I shall be watching you. Keep that in mind.
MID_EV12_027_m01_026: It seems we've attracted attention—and from such an\nunwanted quarter.
MID_EV12_027_m01_027: He is of the Church of Seiros—and at the highest\nechelons, as well.
MID_EV12_027_m01_028: Hmm... Perhaps a cardinal? Perhaps even greater\nthan that.
MID_EV12_027_m01_029: If so... Why do you hide? You are both of the Church\nof Seiros. Should he not be your ally?
MID_EV12_027_m01_030: I have my reasons. Certain people are better avoided\nthan encountered.
MID_EV12_027_m01_031: No need to concern yourself, but I can explain,\nif you insist.
MID_EV12_027_m01_032: Having said that... I would appreciate if you would\navoid him. At all costs.
MID_EV12_027_m01_033: I suggest you tell him.
MID_EV12_028_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_028_m01_001: You there! All of you! I need you for a sec!
MID_EV12_028_m01_002: You're the clan House Lamine, right?
MID_EV12_028_m01_003: Hearing it spoken in this way, I again feel, viscerally,\nhow utterly misapplied this name truly is.
MID_EV12_028_m01_004: Well, I like it! I don't see a problem at all.
MID_EV12_028_m01_005: I may not have a home, but at least I have a house!
MID_EV12_028_m01_006: I recognize you. You were at the temple.
MID_EV12_028_m01_007: Oh? I was, was I? How interesting. Ahaha! I don't\nremember that at all.
MID_EV12_028_m01_008: You seem to have earned the trust of the Divine\nSovereign. So why pretend otherwise?
MID_EV12_028_m01_009: Shhh! Put a lid on all that! I'm trying to avoid\ndrawing attention here!
MID_EV12_028_m01_010: Very well.
MID_EV12_028_m01_011: Ahem! Now, listen! The date and opponent for your\nqualifier have been set.
MID_EV12_028_m01_012: Take this. It has all of the details, so read it carefully.
MID_EV12_028_m01_013: <TLP>House Lamine\n\nMatch: Second Qualifier of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Silver Knights of Tellus\nLeader: Alexandra\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}
MID_EV12_028_m01_014: Make sure you're prepared for your match, or you'll\nregret it. There's no time to waste!
MID_EV12_028_m01_015: You did make it through the first round—well done—\nso I don't need to explain things again, do I?
MID_EV12_028_m01_016: But feel free to ask me if you have any questions!
MID_EV12_028_m01_017: <NCA>Ask about teammates.
MID_EV12_028_m01_018: <NCB>Don't ask anything.
MID_EV12_028_m01_019: <ACA>Will we be asked again to fight alongside\nanother clan?
MID_EV12_028_m01_020: <ACA>It'll be the same as last time, but as for the details...\nYou'll have to wait for the results of the qualifiers.
MID_EV12_028_m01_021: <ACA>They do say that chance is an element of the games.\nPerhaps this is how it is introduced.
MID_EV12_028_m01_022: <ACB>I have no query.
MID_EV12_028_m01_023: Don't forget that I'll be cheering for you, so...\nGood luck!
MID_EV12_028_m01_024: Seems our opponent is pretty well-known around\nDagsion. She's rich, and people are talking.
MID_EV12_028_m01_025: She's well-bred, capable, and pretty. Men are falling\nfor her left and right. Or so I hear.
MID_EV12_028_m01_026: Sounds like a perfect lady... Not like me at all.
MID_EV12_028_m01_027: I grew up in a tiny village way out in the middle of\nnowhere. In a city like this, I'm just a stray cat.
MID_EV12_028_m01_028: I won't have you talking about yourself that way! You\nshould be proud of who you are.
MID_EV12_028_m01_029: What matters most is your heart. Well, and having\ngood sense when it comes to men...
MID_EV12_028_m01_030: Right now, I don't have eyes for anyone but\nmy Sweetie!
MID_EV12_028_m01_031: Regarding this Alexandra that we're to face...
MID_EV12_028_m01_032: I've heard rumors that her strategy for winning is...\nshall we say...deficient in scruples.
MID_EV12_028_m01_033: Come on, don't beat around the bush!
MID_EV12_028_m01_034: It seems that even before she entered the games,\nshe had a propensity to win by default.
MID_EV12_028_m01_035: I believe we would do well to keep our eyes open to\nany chicanery.
MID_EV12_108_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_108_m01_001: Well, well, well. What are you doing here, all by\nyour lonesome?
MID_EV12_108_m01_035: 
MID_EV12_108_m01_036: 
MID_EV12_108_m01_037: 
MID_EV12_108_m01_002: Don't think you're going anywhere, my friend. We'd\nlike a little chat.
MID_EV12_108_m01_003: Hehehe. We need a favor—an easy one. When the\ntime comes for your next match...don't show.
MID_EV12_108_m01_004: Now, about an excuse...we'll give you one.\nRight now!
MID_EV12_108_m01_005: Let's break an arm or two! Can't fight if you can't\nhold your weapon, can you?
MID_EV12_108_m01_006: A challenge? How droll.
MID_EV12_108_m01_007: Come as one—it matters not.
MID_EV12_108_m01_008: I know none of your faces, yet you challenged me\nas soon as you recognized me.
MID_EV12_108_m01_009: I begin to see how she has been winning all her\nmatches by default.
MID_EV12_108_m01_010: When a group of men threatens a young lady, they\nexpect her to just obey, it seems.
MID_EV12_108_m01_011: Why is it that men like this are so very...stupid?
MID_EV12_108_m01_038: 
MID_EV12_108_m01_039: 
MID_EV12_108_m01_040: 
MID_EV12_108_m01_012: I can't believe it. How are you so strong?
MID_EV12_108_m01_013: Listen, you! Next time you'll be sorry. Mark\nmy words!
MID_EV12_108_m01_014: What? My legs... I can't move! What's wrong with\nme? Help! Help!
MID_EV12_108_m01_015: A word, if you will. Tell me who sent you.
MID_EV12_108_m01_016: Did you think I would allow you to leave? Tell me\nwho ordered this attack.
MID_EV12_108_m01_017: You think you're getting out of here? So very stupid.\nNow, why did you attack me? Who sent you?
MID_EV12_108_m01_018: Please, stop! I can't talk! I'll be killed! You will\ntoo! Please!
MID_EV12_108_m01_019: I find myself unintimidated.
MID_EV12_108_m01_020: In fact, dodging an assassin in Dagda might well\nbe entertaining.
MID_EV12_108_m01_021: You, however, are unneeded. Perish.
MID_EV12_108_m01_022: I care nothing for your fears—or your life. Let me\ntell you whom you ought to truly fear.
MID_EV12_108_m01_023: If you will not tell me what you know, I shall break\nyour arms first, and then your legs.
MID_EV12_108_m01_024: And why stop there? You have many more bones\nto shatter until your lips loosen.
MID_EV12_108_m01_025: Oh, really? You know, I think you might not fully\ngrasp your current situation.
MID_EV12_108_m01_026: I have a suggestion. You tell me who sent you, and\nthen you leave town. Easy as that.
MID_EV12_108_m01_027: No? Wellll...what if I chopped off your ears? Oooh, or\nyour nose? Would that change your mind?
MID_EV12_108_m01_028: Eeek! No! Please—please! I'll talk! I'll spill my guts!
MID_EV12_108_m01_029: So it was just as Fabio suspected.
MID_EV12_108_m01_030: This plan has failed, but I do anticipate whatever is\ncoming next...
MID_EV12_108_m01_031: So my suspicions are confirmed. 
MID_EV12_108_m01_032: She plays the part of a pacifist, but there is a vicious\nstreak underneath.
MID_EV12_108_m01_033: I see. I suppose that makes sense...
MID_EV12_108_m01_034: She's sweetness on the surface but ugliness at the\nbone. Hm, I wouldn't have thought that about her.
MID_EV12_029_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_029_m01_001: Oh my, what have we here? You must be Dietrich!\nAren't you magnificent!
MID_EV12_029_m01_002: I've been terribly curious about you. And now that I\nsee you up close...why, you really are very handsome.
MID_EV12_029_m01_003: I almost want to trade you for Sirocco here!
MID_EV12_029_m01_004: Come now, Miss Leda, I really must insist that\nyou don't...
MID_EV12_029_m01_033: I almost want to trade you for Sirocco here!
MID_EV12_029_m01_034: Come now, Miss Leda, I really must insist that\nyou don't...
MID_EV12_029_m01_005: What do you think, Queen Theodora? Isn't he\nfabulous?
MID_EV12_029_m01_006: I shall withhold judgment. I make a point never to\ngauge a man's merits by his face.
MID_EV12_029_m01_007: I grant he is somewhat handsome, but I see nothing\nremarkable about him otherwise.
MID_EV12_029_m01_008: Your Majesty, you could search all Dagda and never\nfind anyone so fine. My eyes hurt—he's so pretty!
MID_EV12_029_m01_009: That's right! And Sweetie isn't just his looks. He's got\nit all!
MID_EV12_029_m01_010: Take his personality... Deep inside, he's a tender little\nmuffin! Though you might just miss it.
MID_EV12_029_m01_011: Oh, is he now? So, you're a couple?
MID_EV12_029_m01_012: A couple? Well, I mean...that's what I'd like, but...
MID_EV12_029_m01_013: But! I've been meaning to ask! Why...why is it you\ncity girls have such a glow about you?
MID_EV12_029_m01_014: A...glow? Hmm, I don't know about other girls, but\nI do have a skin balm I use. I'm happy to share.
MID_EV12_029_m01_015: If it's no trouble...sure! I'd love to try it!
MID_EV12_029_m01_016: Leda, was it? I should like to try some as well.
MID_EV12_029_m01_017: What you use must be special. The luster of your\nskin was apparent when I first laid eyes on you.
MID_EV12_029_m01_018: Oh, uh, thanks. It's made out in Caelus, so it's not\neasy to find.
MID_EV12_029_m01_019: I can hardly follow this conversation...nor do I wish\nto, I'm afraid. It unsettles me.
MID_EV12_029_m01_020: This convivial atmosphere is antithetical to my\nscholarly mien.
MID_EV12_029_m01_021: I, too, am not suited to this banter. Perhaps my\nsister would... But no, she is quieter.
MID_EV12_029_m01_022: Baw haw haw! Anywhere in the world you get\nsome girls together, it's a party!
MID_EV12_029_m01_023: Way better than a room full of guys, which just\nleaves a bad smell.
MID_EV12_029_m01_024: Look at how she steps outside her status for a\ncarefree moment with other maidens her age.
MID_EV12_029_m01_025: How long has it been since Her Majesty allowed\nherself this? I feel a tear coming to my eye.
MID_EV12_029_m01_026: I am all the more resolved now to hold body and soul\ntogether till the day of Her Majesty's wedding.
MID_EV12_029_m01_027: Yeah, but then you'll say you can't die until you get\nto dandle her grandkids on your knee.
MID_EV12_029_m01_028: How long do you plan to let sappiness keep you\nalive, Bona?
MID_EV12_029_m01_029: Jokes aside, something's been bothering me ever\nsince we got here.
MID_EV12_029_m01_030: I've been hearing water from somewhere this whole\ntime. What's going on there?
MID_EV12_029_m01_031: Ahh. Since you bring it up, I have heard that this\narena is equipped with some sort of water feature.
MID_EV12_029_m01_032: Perhaps the water you've been hearing is connected\nto what they have in store for us.
MID_EV12_030_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_030_m01_001: To the northwest of Dagda, from the sparkling Lir\nSea, the islands of Brigid rear forth like a dragon!
MID_EV12_030_m01_002: In this land wracked with endless turmoil, war broke\nout, five hundred years ago...
MID_EV12_030_m01_003: and we bore witness to the greatest naval battle in\nthe history of Dagda. Surely you must know it!
MID_EV12_030_m01_004: In the year of 875, King Arago the Upright sought to\nregain stability in the northwest sea.
MID_EV12_030_m01_005: He bestowed upon General Gisco the warships of the\nDagdan Empire and sent him into battle.
MID_EV12_030_m01_006: Brigid's seven clans allied and put up a fierce\nresistance. The sea itself became a battlefield!
MID_EV12_030_m01_007: In the Eastern Division, Alexandra and her Silver\nKnights of Tellus shall fight as General Gisco's army!
MID_EV12_030_m01_008: In the Western Division, Queen Theodora and her\nindomitable allies play the role of Brigid's champions!
MID_EV12_030_m01_009: Quiver with anticipation, onlookers, for our epic\nbattle is about to begin!
MID_EV12_030_m01_010: Are you seeing this? There's a sea! They've made a\nsea in the arena!
MID_EV12_030_m01_011: Check it out, boss. They filled the arena like a tub!\nThey even got real ships in here!
MID_EV12_030_m01_012: Wow! It's...it's full of water! The inside of the\ncolosseum is an ocean!
MID_EV12_030_m01_013: It's mind-blowing, is what it is! I didn't know the\ncolosseum was set up for this stuff!
MID_EV12_030_m01_014: Calm yourself, Tobias. The scale of it is unusual, but\nin the end, it is merely another prop.
MID_EV12_030_m01_015: *sigh*
MID_EV12_030_m01_016: As the time for battle draws near, you are...\ncontemplative. Should I be troubled?
MID_EV12_030_m01_017: No. I was pondering that in this land, my fate\nseems bound to the sea.
MID_EV12_030_m01_018: The sea brought you here. And the sea saved\nthe girl.
MID_EV12_030_m01_019: And now these grand games have themselves\ntransformed into a sea...
MID_EV12_030_m01_020: It is intriguing that the maiden we are pitted against\nis a wing soldier.
MID_EV12_030_m01_021: Take care as you move about the ships, lest the\nwater slow you down.
MID_EV12_030_m01_022: Our enemy, of course, has no such restrictions as\nshe strikes from the air.
MID_EV12_030_m01_023: Eh, leave her for our archers. One arrow, and that\nwing soldier will go down like a stone.
MID_EV12_030_m01_024: It will not be so easy, Tobias. Look again at the\nmaiden's shield.
MID_EV12_030_m01_025: Pretty expensive looking. It's a real sweet piece\nof gear.
MID_EV12_030_m01_026: That's the Shield of Zephyrus. It's one of the Arcs.\nIt belongs to Smyrnos, the Spell-Scholar.
MID_EV12_030_m01_027: I've heard that Zephyrus summons the wind, and\nthat it prevents arrows from puncturing deeply.
MID_EV12_030_m01_028: An Arc... They are said to rival the sacred weapons\nof Fódlan, as I recall.
MID_EV12_030_m01_029: I believe I do not have to further explain just how\npowerful it may be.
MID_EV12_030_m01_030: So she would be weak to arrows, but that takes care\nof that. Looks like an uphill battle to me.
MID_EV12_030_m01_031: So you're saying the girl's got no weaknesses?\nWe might be up a creek here.
MID_EV12_030_m01_032: It sounds as though she's...invincible? This is very\nconcerning indeed.
MID_EV12_030_m01_033: Everything is arranged to our enemy's advantage.\nShe even has the assurance of an Arc.
MID_EV12_030_m01_034: Unbelievable. The favoritism is so obvious. Have\nyou ever seen anything like it?
MID_EV12_030_m01_035: This will be hard going, but I shall not rest until we\nhave clawed our way to victory.
MID_EV12_030_m01_036: Once that is done, we shall hunt down whoever is\npulling this girl's strings.
MID_EV12_030_m01_037: Ooo, great idea! Sounds like fun. Count me in!
MID_EV12_030_m01_038: You'll help us out too, won't you, Dietrich?
MID_EV12_030_m01_039: The circumstances do not dictate my actions. All\nwho face me will fall.
MID_EV12_030_m01_040: Ack...
MID_EV12_030_m01_041: Boss? You alright?
MID_EV12_030_m01_042: Yes... It is nothing. I am fine...for the moment.
MID_EV12_031_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_031_m01_001: *sigh*
MID_EV12_031_m01_002: How intently you watched that match.
MID_EV12_031_m01_003: I gave him the kiss of the underworld. There is no\nmistaking it.
MID_EV12_031_m01_004: Oh, without a doubt. I saw it myself.
MID_EV12_031_m01_005: And yet there he stood, acting of his own free will.
MID_EV12_031_m01_006: Not once has my charm ever failed... Not once.\nUntil now.
MID_EV12_031_m01_007: I have posed as an old woman for so long... Have my\nbody and soul begun to wither?
MID_EV12_031_m01_008: I must have his body for Father. It is his will!
MID_EV12_031_m01_009: Is it? Or is it yours, my sister? Born of your desire...
MID_EV12_031_m01_010: Absurd! I would never!
MID_EV12_031_m01_011: So you haven't even realized it, have you? I've seen\nhow you chase him with your eyes.
MID_EV12_031_m01_012: I know this emotion well, even if you do not. It is\ncalled love.
MID_EV12_031_m01_013: How interesting that you could not identify it...
MID_EV12_031_m01_014: Ironic, isn't it? You placed the kiss upon him, but\nyours is the heart that was stolen.
MID_EV12_031_m01_015: Impossible! Unthinkable! I am not like Yu Phas! I am\nnothing like her!
MID_EV12_031_m01_016: We offer everything we have to Father. What you\nsuggest is...impermissible.
MID_EV12_031_m01_017: Sister, dear... Love is as an illness. You catch it\nunaware, and your heart is stricken.
MID_EV12_031_m01_018: Tsk.
MID_EV12_031_m01_019: I say this out of kindness. Unlike dear Eishet, I do\nnot deny the truth of love.
MID_EV12_031_m01_020: Mahna... You... No...
MID_EV12_031_m01_021: Oh, yes. I have loved. I even bore a child.
MID_EV12_031_m01_022: It came of a scheme I set into motion for Father's\nbenefit, of course. Nothing more.
MID_EV12_031_m01_023: You must be careful. Do not err.
MID_EV12_031_m01_024: If you are swept up by your emotions and lose sight\nof your objective... You will regret it deeply.
MID_EV12_031_m01_025: How I know it. We have all given so much for this\ngreat purpose.
MID_EV12_031_m01_026: Especially you, my sister. The Diadem of the Fanatic\nresides in you, after all.
MID_EV12_031_m01_027: You play a pivotal role in our task of manifesting\nFather in this land once again.
MID_EV12_032_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_032_m01_001: Well done, everyone! It was a bit close there, but\nwe won, and that's all that matters.
MID_EV12_032_m01_002: Where'd the queen go? I didn't even notice when she\nslipped away!
MID_EV12_032_m01_003: She and her entourage retired to a private chamber.\nThe situation seems dire.
MID_EV12_032_m01_004: You all were impressive, as well. I've never seen that\nmagic before, and what a...strange sword too.
MID_EV12_032_m01_005: It makes me wonder how you came by this kind\nof weaponry.
MID_EV12_032_m01_006: Powers such as mine are hardly something just\nanyone can master.
MID_EV12_032_m01_007: You could say much the same for the sword, in truth.\nFew could wield it... Though...
MID_EV12_032_m01_008: I say that, yet I would hazard that you are one such.\nYour power is akin to Fódlan's Crest of Dominic.
MID_EV12_032_m01_009: Hey. I wanted to thank you all for helping me out\nback there.
MID_EV12_032_m01_010: Should you really be up and about? I appreciate the\nthanks, but it could have waited.
MID_EV12_032_m01_011: I suspect there is more to it than that...
MID_EV12_032_m01_012: Everything that's happened, well, it was all my\nuncle's idea.
MID_EV12_032_m01_013: He wanted me to win the games and attain glory, so\nhe could marry me off to a handpicked nobleman.
MID_EV12_032_m01_014: To tell you the truth, I knew exactly what he\nwas doing.
MID_EV12_032_m01_015: I thought I owed it to my uncle for taking care of me,\nso until now, I've always done as he said.
MID_EV12_032_m01_016: But the way he just spoke to me... He said thanks to\nmy defeat, everything he'd worked for was ruined.
MID_EV12_032_m01_017: Hmm. I knew something didn't seem right, but I'm\nso sorry. That's awful.
MID_EV12_032_m01_018: Who says you have to repay him if it leaves you\nworse off? That's not fair!
MID_EV12_032_m01_019: In a way, it's a good thing. Now I know I'm finally\nready to leave my uncle's house.
MID_EV12_032_m01_020: It's actually quite liberating. So that's why I wanted\nto come here and say thank you.
MID_EV12_032_m01_021: To summon the will to smash your cage and fly free...\nbeauteous.
MID_EV12_032_m01_022: I will pray that your dreams are fulfilled.
MID_EV12_032_m01_023: Don't worry. With your abilities, you'll have no\ntrouble doing well for yourself.
MID_EV12_032_m01_024: But whatever you do, never let another man take\nadvantage of you. Let that resolve be your prize.
MID_EV12_032_m01_025: Thank you, Leda. I won't forget your words or\nyour kindness.
MID_EV12_032_m01_026: And good luck. I'll be cheering you all on.
MID_EV12_032_m01_027: She's putting on a brave face, but I know that's not\nhow she feels inside.
MID_EV12_032_m01_028: It's young women like her who deserve to be happy.\nI just wish I could find some way to support them.
MID_EV12_032_m01_029: I'm glad that worked out... But I can't shake\nthis feeling.
MID_EV12_032_m01_030: I have scarcely seen you like this. Why, pray tell?
MID_EV12_032_m01_031: Well, just look at Alexandra! And it's not just her.\nLeda, Theodora, Mikaela... Everywhere I look!
MID_EV12_032_m01_032: I'm surrounded by amazing women. It's enough to\nmake a girl jealous!
MID_EV12_032_m01_033: Trust me, you're a diamond in the rough yourself.
MID_EV12_032_m01_034: With a little polish, you'll have more attention than\nyou know what to do with.
MID_EV12_032_m01_035: Speaking of polish, this is the skin balm I promised\nyou before the match.
MID_EV12_032_m01_036: Thank you, Leda! And watch out, world! I'm ready\nto blossom!
MID_EV12_032_m01_037: Hehehe. OK, OK...looks like it's time for us to go.
MID_EV12_033_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_033_m01_001: Refining your appearance has merit, of course, but I\nposit that refining your mind has more.
MID_EV12_033_m01_002: Easy for you to say! Do you think I've had time to\nstudy? To learn manners? It isn't so simple!
MID_EV12_033_m01_003: And here I thought you had lately set foot on the\npath to humanity.
MID_EV12_033_m01_004: Wait just a second! Are you saying I'm not even\nhuman now?
MID_EV12_033_m01_005: It's not like I couldn't tell what you think of me, but...\nThat's low, even for you!
MID_EV12_033_m01_006: Yes, well. All living things are driven by instinct. But\nthat which lives purely by instinct is a beast.
MID_EV12_033_m01_007: The social order is formed by draping a veil of reason\nover instinct, so as to live without incident.
MID_EV12_033_m01_008: This behavior can be observed in all manner of\nanimals that live in groups.
MID_EV12_033_m01_009: Negative feelings such as jealousy, insecurity, and\ninvidiousness do dwell within us, I concede.
MID_EV12_033_m01_010: Yet we exert discipline to rid ourselves of them and\nascend toward reason. That is human, and sublime.
MID_EV12_033_m01_011: Indeed, I intuit that your motives are pure, and thus I\nfeel I must set aside my quarrel with you in this case.
MID_EV12_033_m01_012: Invidiousness? What does that even mean? Do you\nwant me to understand you or not?
MID_EV12_033_m01_013: In this instance, I mean only to praise you.
MID_EV12_033_m01_014: Ughhh.
MID_EV12_033_m01_015: Esmeralda, I don't have a formal education either.\nAnd sometimes I struggle.
MID_EV12_033_m01_016: Because of that, I want my daughter to learn so she\nwon't have to go through what I went through.
MID_EV12_033_m01_017: I guess what I'm saying is...it's not going to be\nany fun...
MID_EV12_033_m01_018: But you can learn from Fabio. He understands all\nkinds of things about the world.
MID_EV12_033_m01_019: I don't think I've ever met anyone cleverer than him.
MID_EV12_033_m01_020: I wish I could argue with you...but I can't.
MID_EV12_033_m01_021: Ahaha.
MID_EV12_033_m01_022: Sweetie? Did you actually laugh? You laughed! And\na little smile too.
MID_EV12_033_m01_023: Now that you mention it...yes. You may be right.
MID_EV12_033_m01_024: Ech... Hmhmhm.
MID_EV12_033_m01_025: {SetColor=Gray}All this, and I still cannot acknowledge even one of\nthem as human.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_033_m01_026: {SetColor=Gray}You retain not even a scrap of the greatness of your\nancestors, and you cling to a goddess who is your foe.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_033_m01_027: {SetColor=Gray}All you do is quarrel over the meager fodder\nscattered across the floor of this cage of lies.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_033_m01_028: {SetColor=Gray}Could you call this behavior anything else than that\nof beasts?{SetColor=Default}